{
  "case_id": "2024-24a884",
  "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Government is likely to succeed on the merits of its claim that the District Courts lacked authority to issue universal injunctions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0000-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "sider Scott v. Donald, where the plaintiff successfully challenged the constitutionality of a law on which state offcials had relied to confscate alcohol that the plaintiff kept for personal use. See 165 U. S. 107, 109 (statement of case); id., at 111\u2013112 (opinion of the Court). Although the plaintiff sought an injunction barring enforcement of the law against both himself and anyone \u201cwhose rights [were] infringed and threatened\u201d by it, the Court permitted only relief benefting the named plaintiff."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "The Coalition to Defend Affrmative Action et al.",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0000-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Briefs of amici curiae urging the denial of the applications were fled in all cases for B. A. M. N. (The Coalition to Defend Affrmative Action et al.) by Shanta Driver;"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0000-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice Barrett delivered the opinion of the Court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0000-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The applications before us concern three overlapping, universal preliminary injunctions entered by three different District Courts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Plaintiffs",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0001-0000",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The plaintiffs fled suit, alleging that the Executive Order violates the Fourteenth Amendment's Citizenship Clause, \u00a7 1, as well as \u00a7 201 of the Nationality Act of 1940, 54 Stat. 1138 (codifed at 8 U. S. C. \u00a7 1401)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0001-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Government has now fled three nearly identical applications seeking to partially stay the universal preliminary injunctions and limit them to the parties."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Solicitor General",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "On multiple occasions, and across administrations, the Solicitor General has asked us to consider the propriety of this expansive remedy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Government is likely to succeed on the merits of its argument regarding the scope of relief."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0001-0004",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The answer is no: Neither the universal injunction nor any analogous form of relief was available in the High Court of Chancery in England at the time of the founding."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0001-0005",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Because the universal injunction lacks a historical pedigree, it falls outside the bounds of a federal court's equitable authority under the Judiciary Act."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0002-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Rule 23 requires numerosity (such that joinder is impracticable), common questions of law or fact, typicality, and representative parties who adequately protect the interests of the class. Fed. Rule Civ. Proc. 23(a)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0002-0002",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Thus, under the Judiciary Act, federal courts lack authority to issue them."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0003-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Finally, the Government must show a likelihood that it will suffer irreparable harm absent a stay."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Government's applications to partially stay the preliminary injunctions are granted, but only to the extent that the injunctions are broader than necessary to provide complete relief to each plaintiff with standing to sue."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0003-0000",
      "kind": "concurrence",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Court today holds that federal courts may not issue so-called universal injunctions. I agree and join in full."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0003-0001",
      "kind": "concurrence",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I join the opinion of the Court but write separately to note two related issues that are left unresolved and potentially threaten the practical signifcance of today's decision: the availability of third-party standing and class certifcation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0004-0000",
      "kind": "concurrence",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In justiciable cases, this Court, not the district courts or courts of appeals, will often still be the ultimate decisionmaker as to the interim legal status of major new federal statutes and executive actions\u2014that is, the interim legal status for the several-year period before a fnal decision on the merits."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0004-0002",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "applications for stays or injunctions with respect to major new federal statutes and executive actions. Deciding those applications is not a distraction from our job. It is a critical part of our job."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0005-0000",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Citizenship Clause provides that \u201c[a]ll persons born or naturalized in the United States and subject to the jurisdic-\ntion thereof, are citizens of the United States and of the State wherein they reside.\u201d U. S. Const., Amdt. 14, \u00a7 1."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0006-0003",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The universal injunctions of the Citizenship Order ft frmly within that tradition. The right to birthright citizenship is \u201cclear,\u201d the Citizenship Order is an \u201c `illegal act,' \u201d and without the \u201c `preventive process of injunction,' \u201d the right will be \u201c `irreparably injured.' \u201d Arthur v. Oakes, 63 F. 310, 328 (CA7 1894) (Harlan, J.) (describing standard for when an injunction should issue)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0008-0000",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 83,
        "start": 83
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "As an initial matter, the Government never raised those narrower injunctions to the District Courts, meaning it forfeited them. That is what the First Circuit expressly held, 131 F. 4th, at 43 (\u201cdeclining to consider\u201d those alternatives because they were \u201craised for [the] frst time . . . in support of stay pending appeal of preliminary injunction\u201d), and the majority does not dispute the point."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0008-0001",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 84,
        "start": 84
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Such a system would also be incompatible with federal law. Some statutes, like those governing Medicaid and Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program (SNAP) benefts, require States to give benefts only to applicants with a Social Security number and to use those numbers for certain administrative purposes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0008-0002",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 85,
        "start": 85
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Inexplicably, however, the Court declares that, for the associational and individual respondents, injunctions enjoining the Government from enforcing the Citizenship Order against them (and only them) would have suffced."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0008-0005",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "United States, for it purports to strip citizenship from the children of parents legally present on a temporary basis."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0008-0006",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 89,
        "start": 89
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Appeals holding the Citizenship Order unlawful (except with respect to the plaintiffs in the suit), even within the relevant Circuit."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0008-0007",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 90,
        "start": 90
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "applications challenged only the scope of the preliminary injunctions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0008-0008",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 91,
        "start": 91
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That mechanism may provide some relief, but it is not a perfect substitute for a universal injunction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0008-0009",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 92,
        "start": 92
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The rule of law is not a given in this Nation, nor any other. It is a precept of our democracy that will endure only if those brave enough in every branch fght for its survival."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0009-0000",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 93,
        "start": 93
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Stated simply, what it means to have a system of govern-\nment that is bounded by law is that everyone is constrained\nby the law, no exceptions. And for that to actually happen,\ncourts must have the power to order everyone (including the\nExecutive) to follow the law\u2014full stop."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0009-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 94,
        "start": 94
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "May\n a federal court in the United States of America order\n the Executive to follow the law?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0009-0002",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 96,
        "start": 96
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The power to compel the Executive to follow the law is particularly vital where the relevant law is the Constitution."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0009-0003",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 102,
        "start": 102
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What I mean by this is that our rights-based legal system can only function properly if the Executive, and everyone else, is always bound by law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fb37a04b11076b76687f6970fbcc6672693c2d9a8f7115cee4ab8eb3c2bf008a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fb37a04b1107-0010-0000",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 103,
        "start": 103
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "has not yet sued carves out a huge exception\u2014a gash in the basic tenets of our founding charter that could turn out to be a mortal wound."
    }
